    <h1>Announcement Regarding Recent DMCA Takedowns and Service Disruptions</h1>
    <p>Over the past several weeks, arras.io has received multiple DMCA takedown notices from 3AM Experiences LLC, the owner of diep.io. These notices have since resulted in the deletion of our official Discord server and most proxy sites, as well as intermittent outages affecting various game servers.</p>
    <p>We want to provide a clear and transparent summary of what we know, what we have been told, what we believe regarding the claims being made, and what steps we are currently taking to resolve the situation.</p>
    <h2>What we know</h2>
    <p>Between mid-November and mid-December, multiple copyright-related takedown actions were taken against arras.io across several platforms:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><span><span><b>Thu, Nov 13, 10:07 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>Copyright infringement notices from Discord, disabling of various bots associated with the arras.io Discord server <i>(notice not provided by Discord)</i></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Mon, Dec 1, 8:13 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>Copyright infringement notice from Discord, deleting of the official arras.io Discord server <i>(notice not provided by Discord)</i></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Tue, Dec 2, 11:27 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>DMCA notice to Netlify, removing the Netlify proxy site <a href="2025-12-02-netlify.txt">(link)</a></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Wed, Dec 3, 1:31 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>DMCA notice to Google, removing the Google Sites proxy site <a href="https://lumendatabase.org/notices/75068228">(link 1)</a> <a href="https://lumendatabase.org/notices/75139148">(link 2)</a></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Wed, Dec 3, 4:25 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>DMCA notice to various game servers <a href="2025-12-03-cloudflare.txt">(link)</a></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Sat, Dec 6, 9:23 AM UTC</b>: </span><span>DMCA notice to game servers <i>(repeat of previous notice)</i></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Wed, Dec 10, 3:02 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>DMCA notice to game servers <i>(repeat of previous notice)</i></span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Thu, Dec 11, 3:10 PM UTC</b>: </span><span>DMCA notice to game servers <i>(repeat of previous notice)</i></span></span></li>
    </ul>
    <p>Beginning on December 3, DMCA notices submitted by 3AM Experiences LLC have repeatedly targeted various arras.io game servers. These repeated submissions have caused intermittent and unpredictable service disruptions as hosting providers temporarily disable or review affected infrastructure.</p>
    <h2>What we've been told</h2>
    <p>Representatives associated with 3AM Experiences LLC have stated that they did not personally issue the DMCA notices, and that the notices were issued as part of intellectual property enforcement handled by an external IP protection firm. It is our understanding that this firm refers to MGL LLP, a Los Angeles-based law firm specializing in video game intellectual property.</p>
    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <p>We respect intellectual property law and the rights of developers to protect their original creative works. However, based on our understanding of U.S. copyright law and longstanding legal precedent, we believe the claims raised in these DMCA notices would face significant legal challenges if litigated. In particular:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>U.S. copyright law does not extend to abstract game mechanics, rules, systems, upgrade paths, or functional gameplay concepts.</li>
      <li>Many of the similarities cited relate to mechanics or genre conventions common across .io games and browser-based multiplayer games generally.</li>
      <li>Arras.io does not use or distribute diep.io source code, artwork, or proprietary assets, and all game logic and visuals are independently implemented.</li>
      <li>Simple geometric shapes and basic visual primitives, such as circles, rectangles, and regular polygons, are not copyrightable and are widely used across interactive software and games.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Additionally, with respect to our community Discord server, even if the underlying copyright claims were assumed to be valid, hosting a community space where players discuss the game, share screenshots, or post gameplay clips is generally considered fair use under U.S. law. Such content is transformative, non-commercial, and does not substitute for or diminish the market for the original work.</p>
    <h2>What we're doing</h2>
    <p>We are actively working to resolve this situation and restore affected services:<p>
    <ol>
      <li><span><span><b>Discord</b>: </span><span>We have submitted counter-notifications and appeals to Discord and are continuing to communicate with them in an effort to reinstate our official community server. In the meantime, members of the community have set up <a href="https://discord.gg/xXfAXB5VnC">an unofficial Discord server</a> so players can stay in touch. Note that this server is not operated by arras.io.</span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Hosting providers</b>: </span><span>We are working closely with our hosting and infrastructure providers to respond to DMCA notices and minimize service disruption.</span></span></li>
      <li><span><span><b>Diep.io</b>: </span><span>We are currently in direct communication with representatives of 3AM Experiences LLC. As part of those discussions, we have been asked to sign a non-disclosure agreement, which we are reviewing carefully.</span></span></li>
    </ol>
    <p>Our priority is to restore stability for players and the community while handling this matter transparently, professionally, and responsibly. We will continue to provide updates as new information becomes available.</p>
